Fired when the user right-clicks this element, just before the context menu is opened.
            Allows building or replacing the menu dynamically without assigning .

Usage: set  to a fresh
             instance, or set 
            to  to suppress the menu entirely.

Subscribing to this event automatically wires up the right-click handler, so you do
            not need to also set  if you only use this event.

Example:

            element.ContextMenuRequested += (s, e) =>
            {
                var m = new MGContextMenu(window, "");
                m.AddButton("Option A", _ => DoA());
                e.Menu = m;
            };

